<article class="env-lemma" id="0A4P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A4P">Lemma <span data-tag="0A4P">69.9.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be an étale morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $Z \subset Y$ be a closed subspace such that $f^{-1}(Z) \to Z$ is an isomorphism of algebraic spaces. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{H}^ q_ Z(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{H}^ q_{f^{-1}(Z)}(f^{-1}\mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> as abelian sheaves on $Z = f^{-1}(Z)$ and we have $H^ q_ Z(Y, \mathcal{F}) = H^ q_{f^{-1}(Z)}(X, f^{-1}\mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Because $f$ is étale an injective resolution of $\mathcal{F}$ pulls back to an injective resolution of $f^{-1}\mathcal{F}$. Hence it suffices to check the equality for $\mathcal{H}_ Z(-)$ which follows from the definitions. The proof for cohomology with supports is the same. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>